# Direct Attrs (No Mapping Types)

Prefer passing the domain object as `attrs` on `segFactory` / `cardFactory`. Do not introduce parallel `*CardAttrs` / `*SegAttrs` types or mapper functions that copy domain fields into a snapshot.

When domain fields are `Property<T>`, keep the Property on attrs and read `.value` at use sites. Do not flatten into plain numbers and sync snapshots back onto the card.

## Correct

```typescript
export interface Lesson {
  readonly id: number;
  readonly weekday: Property<number>;
  readonly hour: Property<number>;
  // ...
}

cardFactory({
  typeName: "LessonCard",
  attrs: lesson,
  selfPos: {
    WeekdaySeg: (place) =>
      place.nested.find((it) => it.attrs.hour === lesson.hour.value),
  },
});

// At selection / getValue sites:
weekday: lesson.weekday.value,
hour: lesson.hour.value,
```

Also correct: attrs that **are** the domain type (`Group`, `Lesson`), and small inline literals when there is no domain object (`{ dateIso }`, `{ text: "Id" }`).

```typescript
segFactory({ typeName: "GroupSeg", attrs: group });
cardFactory({ attrs: { text: "Id" }, renderer: TEXT_RENDERER });
```

## Incorrect

```typescript
export type LessonCardAttrs = {
  readonly id: number;
  weekday: number;
  hour: number;
};

function lessonCardAttrs(lesson: Lesson): LessonCardAttrs {
  return {
    id: lesson.id,
    weekday: lesson.weekday.value,
    hour: lesson.hour.value,
  };
}

cardFactory({
  typeName: "LessonCard",
  attrs: lessonCardAttrs(lesson),
});

// Then syncLessonCardAttrs to keep the snapshot in sync — avoid this.
```

See [Factory API](factory-api.mdc) for `segFactory` / `cardFactory` usage.
